boolean result = (x != 0) && (10 / x > 1);', 'Because the left operand of && is false, Java skips evaluating the right operand entirely, avoiding the division by zero.', 'medium', 75, ARRAY['short-circuit evaluation', 'boolean expressions'], 'Believing Java always evaluates every operand of a Boolean expression.', null, true)
  returning id
